  "headline": "Conversion Rate fell 7.2% (-0.0057) across the focal window.",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "We evaluated the -7.2% (-0.0057) overall shift in Conversion Rate using difference-in-differences, placebo timing, and control group stability tests.",
      "tier_from": "headline_tier"
    },
    {
      "text": "Localization isolate the top effect in North region, Web channel, Personal Care category, which accounts for 131.5% of the total decline across a support size of 3822.",
      "tier_from": "localization[0]"
    },
    {
      "text": "In primary driver testing, this North Web Personal Care segment moved -9.5% versus 0.0% in the control segment (z=-4.8).",
      "tier_from": "drivers[0]"
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver survived placebo timing checks with a 3.3pp diff-in-diff against a 2.0pp noise standard deviation, though dose response testing was inconclusive.",
      "tier_from": "drivers[0]"
    },
    {
      "text": "A rival hypothesis for the broader Personal Care category was also tested, showing a treated movement of -9.5% versus -2.2% in control (z=-3.7).",
      "tier_from": "drivers[1]"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Personal Care category rival driver survived placebo timing with a 2.0pp difference against 2.0pp noise std, while its control segment moved -2.2%.",
      "tier_from": "drivers[1]"
    },
    {
      "text": "Additionally, North region Web Small Appliances represents 129.0% of the overall decline across 3508 sample observations.",
      "tier_from": "localization[1]"
    },
    {
      "text": "Falsification testing ruled out a broader North region confound, where treated moved -2.6% versus 0.0% in control (z=-1.3).",
      "tier_from": "rejected_hypotheses[0]"
    },
    {
      "text": "A broader Web channel confound was similarly rejected after treated moved -2.6% versus 0.0% in control (z=-1.3).",
      "tier_from": "rejected_hypotheses[1]"
    },
    {
      "text": "Growth should apply checkout incident response to recover the 0.0057 gap, tracking conversion rate over 14 days to confirm recovery within 2% of expected baseline.",
      "tier_from": "action"
    }
  ]
